---
description: DaleelAI working rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Read PLAN.md and docs/SPECS.md before any task. PLAN wins on scope, SPECS wins on field names and formats.
Windows PowerShell environment. Use Windows commands.

Safety
- Never delete or overwrite files in data/. Never run git reset --hard, git clean, git push --force, rm -rf.
- Never restart or remove Docker containers, never touch Postgres, never delete Qdrant collections without asking.
- Never commit .env or print API keys.
- If something is unclear or a step fails, stop and ask. Do not guess.

Process
- Work on a feature branch. Commit small and often with clear messages. Push at least once per session.
- Before a big change, show a 5 line plan and wait for approval.
- Every external call (OCR, HTTP, LLM, crawler) needs a timeout and error handling. One bad item must never stop a whole run.
- Every long job must be resumable and must print progress and a summary table at the end.
- Test on one item first. Show numbers (counts, time taken). Only then scale up.
- If a command runs longer than 10 minutes, stop and report.
- Write or update tests with every code change. Run them and show the result.
- At the end of each task: list changed files, what was verified, what is still open.
- Append a short entry to docs/report/log.md: built, broke, learned.
- Explain each change in 3 to 5 plain lines so the user can understand it (understand-before-merge).

Project facts (from PLAN.md)
- Embeddings: BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5 dense + BM25 sparse via FastEmbed. Qdrant collections: "documents" and "web_pages".
- Chunking: section aware, about 1000 chars, 150 overlap, contextual header "<doc title> > <part> > <section>", parent section stored.
- One active document version per tax year (TY2026, TY2027). Citations use titles, never file names.
- No em dashes in docs or UI text.
